preConditionHook:
// The classic opening-range breakout: once the first openingBars bars of the
// session have fixed the range, a bar closes above its high (long) or below
// its low (short).
//
// Not Breakout or HighestHighBreakout, whose Donchian window MOVES with every
// bar -- the opening-range level is FIXED for the whole session once set, so
// the two fire on different bars from mid-session onward.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: a session starts when the
// wall-clock close date changes -- day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)),
// the same slicing CloseWithinAtrOfVwap uses and the same boundary the xxxD
// family carries (EL_Date_Probe.txt: the bar's closing date, no session-date
// reconstruction). The session's running values and a bars-into-session
// counter live in locals reset on that change; SessionOpeningRange is inlined
// rather than referenced, as the corpus does with named composites.
//
// firstCrossOnly = 0 (default) fires on EVERY bar closing beyond the level;
// 1 fires only on the bar that FIRST crosses it. Only measurement will say
// which pays, so the flag carries both.
//
// The bar on which barsIn reaches openingBars is still part of the range and
// its own high is already in orHigh, so el_gt(close[0], orHigh) cannot hold
// on it: the test is >= openingBars and the first bar that can fire is
// openingBars + 1.
//
// WARM-UP: barsIn, orHigh and orLow start at 0 exactly as the EasyLanguage
// variables do, so if the first calculated bar falls mid-session orLow stays
// 0.0 until the first date change and the short side cannot fire. That is
// EL's behaviour and it is mirrored, not corrected.
//
// EL does not short-circuit and C++ does; every operand here is a plain read
// with no side effect and close[1] is always in range, so the two cannot
// diverge. Intraday bars only.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    barsIn = 1;
    orHigh = high[0];
    orLow = low[0];
} else {
    barsIn = barsIn + 1;
    if (barsIn <= (int)openingBars) {
        if (el_gt(high[0], orHigh)) orHigh = high[0];
        if (el_lt(low[0], orLow)) orLow = low[0];
    }
}
orBreakUp = el_ge((double)barsIn, openingBars) && el_gt(close[0], orHigh)
    && (el_eq(firstCrossOnly, 0.0) || el_le(close[1], orHigh));
orBreakDn = el_ge((double)barsIn, openingBars) && el_lt(close[0], orLow)
    && (el_eq(firstCrossOnly, 0.0) || el_ge(close[1], orLow));
